// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//! battmem.resource's functions: a few hundred bits of settings kept where
//! no file has to be read to get them - memory that a reset leaves alone,
//! where the chip has some, and plain memory where it has none. A
//! resource: no Open or Close, its first function in the first slot. The
//! base comes from OpenResource("battmem.resource").
##include resources/battmem as battmem
##basetype BattMemBase
##name battmem.resource
##bias 0
##public
/// The bits to this task alone, for a read and the write that depends on
/// it; held again by the same task, it is released as often.
void ObtainBattSemaphore()
/// Give the bits back.
void ReleaseBattSemaphore()
/// `length` bits from bit `offset` into `buffer`, from its first byte's
/// bit 0 up; 0, or BATTMEMERR_RANGE when they run past the end.
u32 ReadBattMem([*]u8 buffer, u32 offset, u32 length)
/// `length` bits from `buffer` to bit `offset` on; 0, or BATTMEMERR_RANGE
/// when they run past the end.
u32 WriteBattMem([*]const u8 buffer, u32 offset, u32 length)
##end
